        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-08-27T13:41:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I didn\u0027t understand why we were passing around ASTNodes at first, but I think this is the explanation? We need to support\n\n    `int x\u003d0, y\u003dx;`\n\nThe expression for `y` depends on convertVarDeclaration for `x` having run; otherwise `x` won\u0027t exist in the symbol table.\n\nSo that explains the motivation. I am still not really happy about the outcome here, even now that I understand it. It feels awkward. Is there another way to structure this that could let us pass Expressions?\n\nAlso, it seems strange to introduce a refactor for the benefit of DSL that relies on synthesizing empty AST nodes. Isn\u0027t DSLParser getting rid of ASTNode, fairly soon? What happens at that point?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 424,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 425,
        "endChar": 31
      },
      "revId": "86c72897086f5df3702ab8e3bd53e67f5a62e64c",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
