      "writtenOn": "2021-08-27T13:41:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We shouldn\u0027t rely on friend unless there\u0027s no other choice. Instead, create accessor functions for the things you need. IRGenerator isn\u0027t a public-facing API so it\u0027s harmless and safe to let any part of SkSL inspect the RTHeight fields via an accessor. This limits the exposure to reading-only, and just those fields, instead of full read/write access to every field.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 32,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 39,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "86c72897086f5df3702ab8e3bd53e67f5a62e64c",
